# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions (the asan preset runs UBSan with
# halt_on_error=1). Only the vendored Ghidra decompiler and SLEIGH engine
# (third_party/ghidra, built from build-*/third_party/ghidra/src/cpp) are
# listed: upstream quirks that the Java original shares (docs/bug-scrub.md).
# Never add revkit's own code here; fix it.
#
# Shifts. Ghidra computes masks and extensions with shifts by a varnode's
# size in bits, and varnodes over 8 bytes (AArch64's 128-bit floats, x86's
# vector registers) shift by 64 or more, or by a negative amount
# (calc_mask, SubvariableFlow, RuleAndCommute, sign_extend's `(val << sa) >>
# sa` on negative values, SLEIGH pattern expressions). x86 masks the shift
# count to 6 bits, as Java's long shifts do, so the C++ decompiler computes
# what Ghidra's Java side does; patching each site would diverge from it.
shift-exponent:ghidra/src/cpp/
shift-base:ghidra/src/cpp/
# SLEIGH pattern expressions evaluate a processor's operand arithmetic in
# 64-bit signed integers, wrapping like Java's long.
signed-integer-overflow:ghidra/src/cpp/slghpatexpress.cc
# OperandSymbol::print negates a defining expression's INT64_MIN.
signed-integer-overflow:ghidra/src/cpp/slghsymbol.cc
# ConstTpl's copy constructor copies `select`, which the relative-jump and
# space-id constructors leave unset: an uninitialized enum read whose value
# those constants never use.
enum:ghidra/src/cpp/semantics.hh
# SleighBuilder::buildEmpty casts each operand's defining symbol to
# SubtableSymbol before it checks the symbol's type with a virtual call
# (getType), and only uses it as one once the check passes: the cast of a
# VarnodeListSymbol is a vptr report, never a use. Seen in raw-firmware
# detection's sweeps (python SDK test_detect), part 2 of the scrub.
vptr:ghidra/src/cpp/sleigh.cc
# SleighCompile::checkSymbols (rk-sleigh, compiling revkit's own
# processors at build time) casts every symbol of a scope to LabelSymbol
# before it checks getType() and skips the others: the same cast-then-check
# as buildEmpty's (bug scrub part 3).
vptr:ghidra/src/cpp/slgh_compile.cc
# CircleRange::pushForwardBinary (value-set analysis, reached by inference's
# decompilations in rk-decompd workers) computes the minimum negative as
# the maximum positive plus one, which for 8-byte values is INT64_MAX + 1:
# Java's long wraps there, and the next line sign-extends the result (bug
# scrub part 3).
signed-integer-overflow:ghidra/src/cpp/rangeutil.cc
# RulePtrsubCharConstant::applyOp casts an output's type to TypePointer and
# then checks its metatype, returning before any use when it isn't one: the
# same cast-then-check as above (bug scrub part 3).
vptr:ghidra/src/cpp/ruleaction.cc
